# GitHub will auto-request reviews from the owners listed here. A code
# owner is matched by the last matching pattern. Patterns use the same
# `OWNER` syntax as CODEOWNERS (GitHub docs:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners).
#
# For solo / 2-person projects this lets you funnel security-sensitive paths
# (CI/CD, infra, secrets handling) through a single approver instead of any
# contributor.
#
# Replace @your-handle below with the GitHub handles that should approve
# infra changes. Until that's done, the file is inert.
* @your-handle

# Anything under infra/ or .github/ — including CI/CD definitions and
# deploy workflows — needs an explicit extra reviewer so an unattended
# bot PR cannot silently elevate privileges.
infra/        @your-handle
.github/      @your-handle
scripts/      @your-handle

# Data-engineering hotspots: the notebook performs MERGE upserts against
# the production Azure SQL target table.
databricks/   @your-handle
